<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naumburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naumburg is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It became the seat of a bishopric moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeitz">Zeitz</a> in 1028 and grew into a trading town. Its cathedral, with 13th-century statues of founders such as Uta carved by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg-master">Naumburg Master</a>, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, and the bishopric's lands passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naumburg.jpg" alt="Naumburg" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RealPixelStreet · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naumburger_Dom_Westseite.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
